{#
  ══ THE CHALLENGE STRIP ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  One line saying which challenge an award counts inside. Two states, from
  `ChallengeService::stripFor()`, and one partial — so the award page and the
  nomination form cannot word the same fact two ways:

    joined    "Counts toward Celebrate Nigeria · 6/10"   (the October handoff)
    everyone  "Part of Celebrate Nigeria · 4 of 11 prizes left · Details"
                                                         (the challenge prompt)

  The whole line is the link, so the target is the line and not a word in it. The
  dots are `aria-hidden`: "middle dot" is not something anybody needs read to them,
  and without a separator a screen reader runs the halves together.

  @param strip  the resolver's array, or null for nothing at all
#}
{% if strip %}
<a class="ch-strip{{ strip.joined ? '' : ' ch-strip--long' }}" href="/challenges/{{ strip.slug }}" data-theme="{{ strip.theme }}">
  <span class="ch-strip__t">{{ strip.joined ? 'Counts toward' : 'Part of' }} {{ strip.title }}</span>
  {#- The separator travels WITH what it introduces: on a narrow phone the title wraps,
      and a dot left at the end of the first line reads as a mistake. -#}
  <span class="ch-strip__m"><span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span class="ch-strip__n">{{ strip.line }}</span>
  {%- if not strip.joined %} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span class="ch-strip__go">Details</span>{% endif %}</span>
</a>
{% endif %}
